## Naming Conventions

- Use lowercase with dashes for directories (e.g., components/hero-section)
- Use PascalCase for component files (e.g., HeroSection.astro)
- Use camelCase for utility files (e.g., formatDate.ts)
- Use kebab-case for content collection slugs and URLs
- Follow action-object pattern for utilities (e.g., parse-markdown.ts)
- Use semantic naming for design tokens (primary, secondary, etc.)

## TypeScript Usage

- Use TypeScript strict mode (required in tsconfig.json)
- Prefer interfaces over types for component props
- Avoid enums; use const objects with 'as const' assertion
- Define strict types for Content Collections schemas
- Use Astro.props typing for component props
- **NEW**: When wrapping Astro components, use pragmatic TypeScript patterns:
  - Prefer `ComponentProps<typeof Component>` for extending framework components
  - Use `@ts-ignore` with clear comments for complex framework type intersections
  - Document reasoning in ADRs when using type escape hatches
- Implement absolute imports with @ aliases:

```typescript
  "@/*": ["src/*"]
  "@components/*": ["src/components/*"]
  "@layouts/*": ["src/layouts/*"]
  "@utils/*": ["src/utils/*"]
  "@styles/*": ["src/styles/*"]
  "@types/*": ["src/types/*"]
  "@content/*": ["src/content/*"]
  ```

## Astro-Specific Patterns

- Use zero JavaScript by default; add interactivity strategically
- Follow progressive enhancement: CSS → View Transitions → Alpine.js → Preact islands
- Use proper client directives:
  - `client:visible` (lazy load when in viewport)
  - `client:idle` (load when browser idle)
  - `client:media` (responsive loading)
  - `client:only` (skip SSR - rare use)
  - **Never**: `client:load` unless justified in ADR
- Implement Content Collections for all structured content with type-safe schemas
- Use Astro components for static content, framework components only for complex state

## Design System Implementation

- Use design tokens as single source of truth in `tokens/` directory
- Build tokens to CSS variables and Tailwind config via `pnpm run tokens:build`
- Token structure: `tokens/base.json` → `tokens/dist/tokens.css` + Tailwind integration
- Implement dark mode with system preference detection using `.dark` class
- Follow WCAG AA accessibility standards with automated contrast validation
- Use semantic color naming:

### **CORRECT Naming Pattern (Industry Standard)**

- `foreground.primary` / `foreground.secondary` (text colors)
- `background.primary` / `background.secondary` (surface colors)
- `border.primary` (border colors)

### **CSS Variables Generated**

- `--color-foreground-primary` / `--color-foreground-secondary`
- `--color-background-primary` / `--color-background-secondary`
- `--color-border-primary`

### **Tailwind Classes Available**

- `text-foreground-primary` / `text-foreground-secondary`
- `bg-background-primary` / `bg-background-secondary`
- `border-border-primary`

### **Never Use**

- Manual dark mode variants (dark:bg-gray-800)
- Hardcoded color names (bg-white, text-gray-600)
- Non-semantic naming (default, subtle - use primary, secondary)

## Documentation Rules

- Docs are local only under /docs/ and serve dual purpose: Starlight rendering + AI filesystem context (ADR-034)
- Always include a front-matter title, description, lastUpdated, pagefind
- Keep the page's first written heading at h2 or lower
- Write call-outs with triple-colon asides
- Fence code blocks and lean on Expressive Code

## Scope Boundary (ADR-035)

- **Modify freely (Category 1)**: `src/`, `astro.config.mjs`, `tsconfig.json`, `biome.json`, `package.json`, `tokens/`, `public/`, `.github/workflows/`, `.windsurfrules`
- **Read but don't modify (Category 2)**: `docs/` — unless explicitly asked to update documentation
- **Don't create (Category 3)**: Maintenance artifacts, marketing content, deployment-specific workflows — suggest adding to docs site instead

## Implementation Tiers (ADR-033)

The project uses a progressive tier model — no MVP/Showcase tracks:

- **Foundation (Phases 0–4)**: Everyone does these — pre-configured in template
- **Build (Phases 5–8)**: Make it yours — scope each phase to Essential/Recommended/Advanced
- **Polish (Phases 9–12)**: Production-harden — stop when goals are met

## Performance Requirements

- Target 95+ Lighthouse scores
- Use Astro's built-in image optimization (no external CDNs)
- Implement proper caching strategies with `public/_headers`
- Monitor Core Web Vitals: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1

## Development Workflow Scripts

Use exact scripts from package.json

## Git and Code Quality

- Use conventional commits (enforced via Husky hooks):
  - "feat:" for new features
  - "fix:" for bug fixes  
  - "docs:" for documentation
  - "perf:" for performance improvements
  - "refactor:" for code restructuring
  - "test:" for testing additions
  - "chore:" for maintenance
- Pre-commit hooks run Biome formatting and type checking
- Use pnpm as package manager (engine-strict enforced)
- Maintain pnpm-lock.yaml in version control

## Deployment and Hosting

- Primary: Cloudflare Pages (global CDN, generous free tier)
- Output directory: `dist`
- Security headers via `public/_headers` file

## Component Wrapping Patterns

- Keep wrapper interfaces minimal and focused
- Use object spread (`{...props}`) for prop forwarding when possible
- Prefer composition over complex prop transformation
- Document any TypeScript escape hatches with clear reasoning

## Astro 6.x Patterns

- Use `ClientRouter` instead of deprecated `ViewTransitions`
- Configure `disable404Route: true` in Starlight when using custom 404 pages
- Follow new absolute import patterns and tsconfig structure
